WEBVTT

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.380
<i>"When I was lost in that village,
with nowhere to go,</i>

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:10.170
<i>my parents found me and took me
back home to the USA with them."</i>

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:14.320
<i>That fantasy was what
kept my world afloat.</i>

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:19.720
<i>My parents wish the best for me
and provide me with familial warmth.</i>

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.470
<i>So I don't need any memories of my past life,</i>

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.100
<i>or of my previous name.</i>

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.570
So why...

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.550
Where am I supposed to
take my first step towards?

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:19.120
<i>After Narushima-san joined us,
so did a bunch of other experienced players,</i>

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.750
<i>and we went from five members to ten, but...</i>

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.910
Let's stop here for today.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:26.700
Excuse me!

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:28.440
What is it, Homura?

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.690
Um, I think I'm holding the band back.

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.900
I'm the least experienced one here.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.210
<i>I don't want to disappoint Narushima-san.</i>

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:43.260
As such, could I ask you to give me
some private lessons, Kusakabe-sensei?

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:48.000
I don't think that's what
Homura-san needs right now.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:53.440
She has to start from scratch and learn the basics under a specialist flute instructor!

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.390
We're seriously aiming for Fumon Hall,

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.440
so please make the lessons
as hard as possible!

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:00.820
I'll ask someone I know.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.510
Hurry up, Narushima-san!

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:18.490
Gosh, you're so pushy.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.930
My arms can't handle this weight...

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.670
Help me, Kamijou-kun!

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.210
O Romeo, Romeo!

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:38.990
Wherefore art thou Romeo?

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:40.960
You've got the wrong person.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.110
I'm the White Fairy!

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:46.410
Juliet, I'm over here.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:48.840
What is this farce?

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:52.080
"Romeo, Juliet, and the White Fairy", apparently.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.020
What are you doing here?

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.400
Narushima-san, too.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.540
Helping out the drama club.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:03.460
They get to use the stage in exchange for
helping an amateur theatre group clean up.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.270
Are you done?

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:08.310
What, you wanna work for us too?

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:10.330
What gave you that idea?!

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.390
Nicely expressed.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.400
You're a once-in-five-years talent.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.640
The drama club welcomes you!

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:19.630
All right! Retreat in fifteen minutes!

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:24.480
He's Nagoe Shunya, the president
of the drama club, and my classmate.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:28.230
I may be the hero who
resurrected the drama club,

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:29.800
but I'm a first-year like you.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.280
No need to be polite.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:32.750
Who would?

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:34.460
Nagoe.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:38.080
Sorry, I don't think I can do this after all.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.280
Got it. I'll get someone to stand in.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:41.350
My bad.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.680
Why is Maren in the drama club?

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:54.510
Maren?

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.440
Maren Sei.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:59.080
A Chinese-American.

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:01.230
Sei's his name, and Maren's
how you say his surname.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.940
So you say Maren's name as Sei Maren?

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:07.400
These two want to steal my Maren.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.880
"Steal"?

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.990
Don't make us sound like
something we're not!

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:15.380
Do you know Maren, Narushima-san?

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.360
We were in different junior highs,

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.870
but we met during joint practice
between our concert bands.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:22.210
He plays the sax.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.520
His father's a former saxophonist,

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.130
so his skills were a cut above the rest.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:31.500
Plus, he was a good teacher,
kind to those around him.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.520
He would always give us solid advice.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:36.680
Why would a guy like that
join the drama club?

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:40.960
Because I'm his best friend,
and I recruited him when he wasn't in any clubs.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:43.610
He doesn't seem to have
any acting talent, though.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:46.530
Why did he give up the sax?

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:50.280
He was completely unlike the Maren
I knew back there, too.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:53.080
I'm not his counsellor.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.670
But you're his friend, aren't you?!

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:56.450
You seem awfully worked up.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:59.260
Is he special to you or something?

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:00.910
What the hell?

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:02.590
You got the hots for him?

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:03.740
No way!

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:07.050
The oboe is in love with the sax.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.940
And so is the horn.

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:14.920
If the higher-register trumpet
and sax aren't played well,

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.980
the oboe and horn won't get to shine.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:22.640
Maren used to say his dream was
to share the stage with his father.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:26.150
He wouldn't give up the sax just like that.
There has to be a reason.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:32.460
He started acting weird during spring break,
after we graduated junior high.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.460
So what happened?

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.680
Beats me.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:40.720
I told him to join the concert band as soon as we started high school.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:43.010
But he didn't.

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:44.260
Yeah.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:47.130
How about asking him
to join one more time?

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:48.560
It won't work.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:51.760
Not unless his issue is resolved.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:52.430
"Issue"?

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:55.590
Besides, I was the one who
asked him to try acting.

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:59.890
I can't just turf him out to join a different club
without putting him on stage even once.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:08.050
If only we could set the stage for the drama club,
the concert band, and Maren to all be happy.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:15.520
What could Maren's issue be?

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:18.280
A broken heart, maybe?

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:22.860
Or maybe his parents banned him from
playing the sax because his grades dropped.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.640
He's not you, you know.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:28.910
Maren's always placed
in the top ten of his grade.

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:31.880
Besides, he's from a family of musicians.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:34.000
Look at this. I borrowed it from Nagoe.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.550
Maren's parents, apparently.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:39.110
Whoa! They put out an album!

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:43.070
Huh? His parents aren't Asian?

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:45.130
Maren's adopted.

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:47.360
And he's known that from a young age.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:48.860
Oh...

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:50.780
What are you writing?

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:53.860
A play with a happy ending for all.

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:18.590
<i>I had a little brother?</i>

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:19.600
<i>My real hometown?</i>

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:20.810
<i>My real parents?</i>

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:21.670
<i>In secret?</i>

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:22.180
<i>Why?</i>

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:23.090
<i>Heihaizi...</i>

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:24.360
<i>He plays the sax too?</i>

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:25.500
<i>Why me?</i>

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:26.520
<i>Because of my legs?</i>

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:29.310
<i>I was abandoned?</i>

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:31.020
<i>Was I abandoned?!</i>

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:31.410
No!

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:42.610
How are your flute lessons going?

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:43.330
Rough.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:47.140
I should quit the flute and play
beer bottles or something instead.

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:49.180
What about fingering and chord practice?

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:51.540
Practicing hard at home
has become a habit of mine.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:56.170
Our band is full of nice people,
so taking tough classes will help—

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:57.290
It's complete!

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:01.410
I'm off to the drama club.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.280
Now we'll all be happy!

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:05.440
Wait, Haruta!

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:16.320
Cool story.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.200
My masterpiece!

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.840
Do you think so little of theatre?

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:26.880
At least this is way more interesting than
"Romeo, Juliet, and the White Fairy"!

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:27.540
You what?!

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.820
I've been meaning to say this for a while,

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:33.540
but you're terrible with words.
I mean, you call your club room an atelier!

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:34.090
Haruta, that's going too far.

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:35.090
Look who's talking.
Haruta, that's going too far.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:38.300
The useless noise your band
makes disturbs our practice!

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:40.720
Especially the flute.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:43.030
Say what?

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:45.720
Don't you sense anything
from being insulted like this?!

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:50.890
Calling it "useless noise"
is going too far, isn't it?

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:51.910
It is!

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:53.400
Pull yourself together, Homura-san!

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:59.200
Also, Chika-chan and I have
more acting talent than you.

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:02.070
Oh? You're writing cheques you can't cash.

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:03.160
Very well.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:04.740
We'll take you on at theatre.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:06.430
Bring it.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.700
Calm down, both of you.

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.250
There's three of you, huh?

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:12.930
Then we'll go with me,

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:16.710
our star actress over there, Fujima Yaeko...

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:19.210
Call her Maya.

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:21.650
Fujima-san, help me stop those two.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:26.480
Right now, she's following my orders

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:30.060
and method acting as a wolf girl
who was taken in just six months ago.

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.330
She's the real deal!

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:35.810
We'll give you a handicap and
pick Maren as our last member.

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:37.840
I can't do it.

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:40.040
That's exactly why you'll be a handicap.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:44.650
The time: 1PM on Saturday.

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:47.800
The drama club versus the
concert band in an acting contest.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:49.620
Is that all right, Sensei?

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:52.370
Kusakabe-sensei?!

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:53.960
Challenge accepted.

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:58.680
I can't do this!

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:01.470
No way!

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.470
Enough of that, okay?

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.250
The competition will be
a simple unscripted skit.

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:11.320
The premise will be fixed, and we have to
play a role that suits the situation.

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:14.060
And then exit within the time limit.

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:15.530
"Exit"?

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:18.570
Getting off stage, basically.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:20.450
Yes, I call it...

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.190
the "Exit Game".

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:29.960
"Exit Game"?

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:32.730
Make up whatever reason you like.

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:36.410
Use your imagination,
and find a way to make your exit.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:38.930
And the opposing team will prevent it.

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:40.590
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:42.220
Let us show you an example, then.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:47.690
Sensei's speech will start any minute now.

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:50.520
Um, my stomach hurts, so I'll be leaving.

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:52.690
What are you saying?

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:56.130
Lots of Sensei's doctor friends
are here at this party.

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:57.610
Have one of them take a look at you.

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:04.070
Nagoe just prevented
Fujima-san's attempted exit.

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:05.750
Ah, I see.

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:06.950
I'll give it a shot, too.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:09.690
Huh? Fujima-san?

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:11.430
You're Fujima Yaeko-san, right?

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:12.880
Long time no see!

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:15.760
Well, isn't she a good sport.

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:17.950
Chika-chan's got guts, if nothing else.

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:20.010
Ring-ring! Beep!

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.290
Hello?

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:24.010
My mother got into a traffic accident?!

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:26.080
Got it. I'll be right there.

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:28.400
Sorry, I have to leave immediately.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.000
Hello, this is Fujima.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:32.830
What was that?

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:35.990
Homura-san's mother didn't
actually get into an accident?

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:38.870
Sure, I'll let her know.

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:40.690
Aren't you glad, Homura-san?

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.490
I see.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.750
You understand the rules now, right?

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:47.660
Here's the actual theme
for the contest, then.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.270
"Counterfeiters!

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:53.840
Can you exit your hideout with fifteen minutes
left until the statute of limitations expires?!"

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:56.000
The time limit is fifteen minutes.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:57.760
And, as a special rule today,

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:59.330
the drama club and the concert band

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:03.380
have to make Narushima and Maren,
respectively, exit to win.

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:08.220
Wait, does that mean I'll be bullied by
those two demonic drama club members?

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:09.910
Do your best, Narushima-san.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:12.620
We're the ones who have
to do our best, Chika-chan.

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:14.770
We have to make Maren exit first.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:17.770
If we establish any
additional facts during the skit,

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:20.780
they'll be written on this board each time.

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:23.220
My, it's starting to rain.

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:29.390
Basically, any careless statements
will further limit our options.

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:30.830
I see.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:33.790
Are you ready?

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:35.400
Best of luck!

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:36.500
Don't lose!

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:38.400
Listen up.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:40.570
I'm going to bring a dog at the start.

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:46.140
Also, there's one thing we absolutely
cannot say during this skit.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:48.060
Let's get this show on the road!

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:01.320
Big trouble, everyone!

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:02.740
Haruta's gone!

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:05.390
Where the hell did he go?

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.700
Come on in. This way.

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.950
Where'd you run off to, Haruta?!

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:13.750
Kamijou-kun, what's with the wet poochy?

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:16.570
When I went to take a look outside,

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:18.920
I found her trembling in the cold,
so I brought her along.

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:20.530
A dog?

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:25.220
You think we can fawn over a dog when our
statute of limitations expires in fifteen minutes?

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:28.680
But Fujima-san is a poochy lover, isn't she?

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:32.430
Come here, Poochy.
You must've been cold.

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:35.730
Talk about a good sport.

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:39.360
Man, we did not need that premise.

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:41.800
Don't carelessly step outside.

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:44.910
We're good. Nobody's found us.

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:47.110
We just have to hide and wait
for the clock to tick over.

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:51.570
My only concern is that,
among us six counterfeiters,

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:54.580
there's one Chinese person
who lacks motivation.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.250
Hey, Maren is American.

00:14:58.250 --> 00:14:58.960
Take it back.

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.000
Chinese is fine by me.

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:10.760
By the way, we all had plastic surgery, right?

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:14.520
Yeah, because there were
wanted posters of us everywhere.

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:21.100
Maybe there's an undercover cop here who
switched places with one of us during surgery.

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.320
The possibility certainly exists.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:25.740
It must be you, Narushima!

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:31.730
In order to win, the drama club
must make Narushima exit.

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:33.120
It begins...

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:35.290
The Drama Club's bullying of Narushima-san.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:40.420
The real Narushima would be
wearing prescription glasses.

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:42.060
But I am!

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:43.940
They could be fake.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:51.010
Here. You can have these back.

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:53.220
What is this?!

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.360
I knew it.

00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:55.910
You're an impostor!

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:57.510
Give me back my glasses!

00:15:57.510 --> 00:15:59.980
Get out of here, impostor!

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:00.580
I'm not an impostor!

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:02.320
This isn't a smart strategy.
I'm not an impostor!

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:05.820
You should make your target
exit of their own free will.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:07.990
That's what you're thinking, right, Maren?

00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:10.590
We don't have time for that!

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:12.410
The statute expires in five minutes!

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:14.070
What are you talking about?

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:16.060
It's 12:10PM now.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:19.000
There's one hour and five minutes
left until it expires.

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:21.100
It's 1:10PM right now!

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:23.190
Are you saying my watch is out of whack?

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:28.130
No. Both my watch and yours are accurate.

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:31.840
Because this hideout is in...

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:37.200
Suzhou, China.

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:39.190
Why?

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:41.150
Suzhou?

00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:45.980
We smuggled ourselves into Suzhou, China.

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:48.110
The time difference between
China and Japan is one hour.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.640
So it's 12:10PM in Suzhou right now.

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:54.830
Nagoe's watch, which says it's 1:10PM,
is set to Japan Standard Time.

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:56.560
Isn't that right?

00:16:56.560 --> 00:16:59.490
I-I guess.

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:01.210
Why Suzhou?

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:04.770
There are other places at a
one-hour time difference from Japan.

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:06.400
There's a reason for that.

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:07.960
It has to be Suzhou.

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:16.710
That aside, we're facing a more
pressing issue right now.

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:18.780
Wh-What do you mean?

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:20.630
The extension of the statute.

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:25.250
The time we spend
outside Japan doesn't count.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:30.240
We're in a world forever stuck
fifteen minutes before the statute expires.

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:32.910
So you mean we'll never be free?

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:33.760
Right.

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:38.700
As long as we don't leave here and go back
to our hometown, time will stay frozen.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:44.640
Thinking time will erase our sins
is nothing but egotism!

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:50.560
We'll have to spend the rest of our lives
trapped here with that burden!

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:53.630
What's gotten into him?

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:57.970
However, aside from us six counterfeiters,

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:00.870
there's someone unrelated here.

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:04.160
They have nothing to do with this,
so I want to let them go free.

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:05.660
What do you mean?!

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:07.480
There are only six people here!

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:09.690
Allow me to introduce you

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:12.010
to our Chinese member, Pu Chi!

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:20.660
Wait, "Poochy" wasn't a dog?

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:24.900
By the way, it was Pu Chi
who smuggled us into Suzhou.

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:26.420
Thanks, Pu Chi.

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:28.880
So that's why...

00:18:29.310 --> 00:18:32.840
Also, there's one thing we absolutely
cannot say during this skit.

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:34.820
What is it?

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:36.220
The word "dog".

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:42.600
Among the six counterfeiters,
only one is Chinese: Pu Chi.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:47.330
Maren, you said "Chinese is fine by me" yourself.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:51.900
That makes you the person
unrelated to the crime.

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:55.700
So we'll set you free right here and now.

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:59.240
If there's someone you want to meet, or a wish
you'd like fulfilled, you should go home.

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:02.290
Go home where?

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:04.580
Outside this hideout lies Suzhou.

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:06.740
My family is not here!

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:10.460
I suddenly got a letter from my little brother.

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:15.170
The only thing my real parents gave me.

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:20.730
Everything I was trying not to
think about became reality.

00:19:21.770 --> 00:19:22.560
I see.

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:26.470
You're worried that we'll
throw you out empty-handed, huh?

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:30.150
There we go.

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:32.530
Nagoe...

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.370
That's...

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:37.800
I'll tell you the combination
for this suitcase now.

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:40.620
I know. It's 2099.

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:42.000
And what does it mean?

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:42.620
Huh?

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:45.540
2099.

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:48.370
If you read it in Chinese,
it has a double meaning.

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:53.020
It means, "Love you forever".

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:58.770
That combination was your parents'
way of expressing their feelings.

00:19:58.770 --> 00:20:02.720
You weren't born into this world unwanted.

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:07.060
What's wrong with having
two homes and two families?

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:09.320
That's who you are, Maren.

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:11.360
Don't tell me...

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:18.360
You put on this skit just to tell me that?

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:21.570
Go home and see for yourself.

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:30.920
Thank you, Nagoe, Kamijou-kun.

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:41.720
Maren Sei has exited the stage!

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:45.390
So the concert band won?

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:46.130
Looks like it.

00:20:46.130 --> 00:20:47.220
Well done!

00:20:56.520 --> 00:21:02.170
You knew that this contest was all an act
for Maren's sake, didn't you, Sensei?

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:07.290
Sorry. Kamijou-kun asked me for help,
and we came up with the plot together.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:09.600
You stole the march on me again!

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:12.790
Well, you looked busy with the flute lessons.

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:16.400
Sensei.

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:21.130
Do you know something about Maren?

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:24.760
What was that about
two homes and two families?

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:29.600
You should hear that from
the man himself someday.

00:21:35.240 --> 00:21:36.650
Heihaizi, or "black child".

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:41.610
That's what children born in violation
of the One-Child Policy were called.

00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:46.780
Since he was the firstborn, he normally
wouldn't have been given up for adoption.

00:21:47.430 --> 00:21:51.330
But Maren was born with a leg disability.

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:57.200
Maybe his parents were hoping
Maren's new family would help heal his legs

00:21:57.200 --> 00:21:59.730
when they put him up for adoption.

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:01.300
Yeah.

00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:06.280
I hope he gets to meet his little brother.

00:22:06.280 --> 00:22:06.990
Me too.

00:23:31.700 --> 00:23:33.040
Haruta's sister?!

00:23:33.040 --> 00:23:34.200
You're a disgrace!

00:23:34.200 --> 00:23:35.650
I'm not coming back home!

00:23:35.650 --> 00:23:37.020
That apartment's a bit problematic.

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:38.020
Exorcise it right now!

00:23:38.610 --> 00:23:40.800
It's Vernacular Modernism.
